=== 3. BETWEEN-pair clustering (A7 at the correct unit), p_lbm=0.80, series of 5 ===
   Within-pair similarity is the SIGNAL and is NOT discounted — the unit is
   the pair. A7 applies BETWEEN pairs: several pairs from one med-chem
   campaign are not independent of EACH OTHER.

   NOTE, and it is why this sweeps concordance too: clustering correlates
   pair DIFFICULTY, and difficulty reaches the outcome only through the
   concordance channel. At concordance=0 it is PROVABLY INERT — a sweep
   there would report a column of identical numbers and measure nothing.

 pairs   conc   icc0.0   icc0.5   icc0.8    delta
-------------------------------------------------
    20    0.0    0.374    0.374    0.374    0.000  INERT
    20    0.3    0.414    0.415    0.421    0.007
    20    0.6    0.494    0.469    0.461    0.033
    40    0.0    0.725    0.725    0.725    0.000  INERT
    40    0.3    0.785    0.786    0.786    0.001
    40    0.6    0.868    0.858    0.857    0.011
    60    0.0    0.880    0.880    0.880    0.000  INERT
    60    0.3    0.928    0.924    0.933    0.009
    60    0.6    0.978    0.979    0.978    0.001

   READ THIS ROW-WISE: the delta column is the cost of clustering. It is
   at most a few points, against A7's 0.95 -> 0.46 for the SIGN test.
   Structural reason: McNemar consumes the SPLIT of discordant pairs;
   clustering perturbs their COUNT without biasing the split.

=== 4. type-I error control (p_lbm == p_base), must sit at or below alpha ===
   n_pairs=20   type-I = 0.0250   (exact test is conservative)
   n_pairs=40   type-I = 0.0265   (exact test is conservative)
   n_pairs=60   type-I = 0.0305   (exact test is conservative)
